ZephCore: backport of upstream zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr 1079b21dcda7
("boards: seeed: commit RRAM write buffer after image load", PR #117961,
merged to main 2026-09-01). Not on v4.4-branch, and no backport requested.

The board's `nrf54l-load` proc enables RRAMC writes with a one-line
(128-bit) write buffer and calls load_image, but never commits the buffer.
The image's final partial line is lost at reset, so those bytes keep
whatever the previously flashed firmware had there. Symptom depends on what
lands in that line: in the XIAO nRF54L15 battery-ADC build it was the
startup value of `sync_evt_pool.__bufs`, and flashing that image over a
debug build bus-faulted at the first BT HCI allocation (BFAR 0xf7ce720d,
the debug image's bytes). Erasing does not help; the lost line then reads
0xFF. Reproduced and fix verified on hardware 2026-09-18.

DROP THIS PATCH once the Zephyr pin contains 1079b21dcda7 (or upstream's
later refactor ca77b788f93a, which moves the proc to
boards/seeed/common/openocd_nrf54l.cfg as `nrf54l_load`). It will then fail
`git apply --check`, which is fatal at configure time.

diff --git a/boards/seeed/xiao_nrf54l15/support/openocd.cfg b/boards/seeed/xiao_nrf54l15/support/openocd.cfg
index 8ec6b496f65a..c0e227ff342e 100644
--- a/boards/seeed/xiao_nrf54l15/support/openocd.cfg
+++ b/boards/seeed/xiao_nrf54l15/support/openocd.cfg
@@ -66,6 +66,9 @@ if {![using_hla]} {
 proc nrf54l-load {file} {
 	mww 0x5004b500 0x101
 	load_image $file
+	# Commit the final partial 128-bit RRAM write line left by load_image.
+	# RRAMC.TASKS_COMMITWRITEBUF @ 0x5004b008.
+	mww 0x5004b008 1
 }
 
 # Define CTRL_AP_NUM explicitly to avoid variable errors
